We still lack a concrete low-level cause behind the repetitive mod_jk/mod_jk2 “workerEnv in error state X” messages. Next I’ll search the full log for any explicit failure/errno/permission/shm/socket/open messages (especially around jk/jk2), and for true Apache restart/startup indicators (Apache/version, resuming normal operations, caught signal). This should confirm whether the mod_jk2 scoreboard/shared-memory layer is failing or if Apache is repeatedly restarting/crashing.
